{"type": "vertex_text", "round": 1, "text": "I have completed the source-fidelity preflight review as requested. The review traced every claim limitation, numbered part, figure description, and statement of structure in the draft application to the affirmative inventor sources provided in `input/disclosure.md` and `input/conversation.md`. The draft was also checked for internal consistency.\n\nThe review found one issue in the textual description of the figures. The brief for FIG. 2 described the path of the cutting-plane lines in a way that asserted a specific, unsupported geometric relationship between internal components of the guide carriages. This constitutes an addition of unsupported technical substance, as the relative placement of these components is a choice of the illustrator, not a feature disclosed by the inventor. A finding has been issued to correct the figure brief by removing the assertion of this specific geometry while retaining the necessary information to locate and identify the cutting-plane lines.\n\nWith this correction, the remainder of the application, including all claims, the detailed description, and the numeral list, is fully supported by the inventor's disclosure and is internally consistent."}
